A play is a sequence, but not used to build a list, it is used to exucute on a sequence list.

<p>There are 4 play operators

<table border=1>

{play}
  <tr>
    <td> {&play:key} </td>
    <td> {$play}     </td>
  </tr>
{/play}

</table>

{block}

{table}

{demo}{sequence range='20..30', push='mySequence'} {/demo}

{demo}{pull mySequence, make,   prime} {$sequence} {/pull}{/demo}

{demo}{pull mySequence, keep,   prime} {$sequence} {/pull}{/demo}

{demo}{pull mySequence, remove, prime} {$sequence} {/pull}{/demo}

{demo}{pull mySequence, flag,   prime} {$sequence} {/pull}{/demo}

{/table}

{/block}
